===== docs/current-state.md =====
     1	# Current state and migration boundary
     2	
     3	Last verified: 2026-07-15.
     4	
     5	## What exists
     6	
     7	The repository builds one SwiftPM macOS 14 executable, `ReluxProxy`, packaged by
     8	shell scripts as a menu bar `.app` and DMG.
     9	
    10	The app:
    11	
    12	- stores SSH host, account, and local SOCKS port in `AppStorage`;
    13	- launches `/usr/bin/ssh -N -C -D 127.0.0.1:<port>` with fail-fast, keepalive,
    14	  timeout, batch-mode, and quiet logging options;
    15	- inherits host aliases, keys, ProxyJump, and other behavior from the user's
    16	  `~/.ssh/config`;
    17	- reports connecting, connected, disconnecting, disconnected, and failed states;
    18	- requires the user to configure a browser or other SOCKS-aware client manually;
    19	- intentionally runs outside the App Sandbox so it can spawn system SSH.
    20	
    21	Tests cover profile validation and exact SSH argument construction. CI runs
    22	`swift test` and builds an ad-hoc-signed universal application bundle.
    23	
    24	Tagged releases import the Relux Works Developer ID certificate, build a
    25	universal app, sign the DMG, notarize and staple it, validate it with Gatekeeper,
    26	publish checksums/provenance, and upload both versioned and stable
    27	`ReluxProxy.dmg` assets.
    28	
    29	## What does not exist
    30	
    31	The current app is not a system VPN and does not contain:
    32	
    33	- iOS targets;
    34	- `NETunnelProviderManager` or packet-tunnel extensions;
    35	- a userspace TCP/IP stack or packetFlow bridge;
    36	- an embedded SSH implementation;
    37	- UDP or system DNS forwarding;
    38	- the remote `relux-relay` executable/protocol;
    39	- shared profile/Keychain state between host and extension;
    40	- Network Extension entitlements or provisioning;
    41	- TestFlight/App Store release automation.
    42	
    43	## Migration boundary
    44	
    45	The planned product in `.spec/` is a new architecture, not an incremental toggle
    46	inside `TunnelController`. Existing source files remain the current SOCKS
    47	product until board-approved migration tasks create the multi-target project.
    48	
    49	During migration:
    50	
    51	- the stable macOS release path must remain reproducible;
    52	- current host/account defaults and user expectations need an explicit migration
    53	  decision;
    54	- the system-SSH implementation may remain as a macOS legacy mode, be replaced,
    55	  or be retired only through a product decision;
    56	- SwiftPM tests and release history must not be silently discarded;
    57	- Network Extension code must not be backported into the current manual app
    58	  without the architecture and entitlement gates in `.spec/validation.md`.

===== docs/project-management.md =====
     1	# Project management
     2	
     3	Relux Proxy uses the private
     4	[`relux-works/skill-project-management`](https://github.com/relux-works/skill-project-management)
     5	tooling. The board is stored locally in `.task-board/` and committed with the
     6	repository. Saved execution plans live in `.planning/`.
     7	
     8	## Workstation setup
     9	
    10	Clone or update the skill source, then run its canonical setup command:
    11	
    12	```sh
    13	git clone git@github.com:relux-works/skill-project-management.git \
    14	  ~/src/skill-project-management
    15	
    16	cd ~/src/skill-project-management
    17	./scripts/setup.sh \
    18	  --project-dir /path/to/relux-proxy \
    19	  --mode local \
    20	  --board-dir .task-board \
    21	  --bootstrap-local-agents
    22	```
    23	
    24	The command installs `task-board`, registers the project-management skill, and
    25	creates the repo-local agent runtime. `.agents/`, `.claude/`, `.codex/`, and
    26	`.local/` are generated machine-local directories and are intentionally ignored.
    27	
    28	Verify the setup from the repository root:
    29	
    30	```sh
    31	agents-infra doctor local "$PWD"
    32	task-board q --format compact 'project_config(); summary()'
    33	task-board validate
    34	```
    35	
    36	## Planning contract
    37	
    38	- Product and architecture requirements are source-controlled under `.spec/`.
    39	- Epics, stories, tasks, dependencies, and acceptance criteria are managed only
    40	  through `task-board`; never edit `.task-board/` files by hand.
    41	- A story is implementation-ready only after it has atomic child tasks with
    42	  verifiable acceptance criteria and explicit dependencies.
    43	- Canonical phases come from `task-board q 'plan(...)'`; saved snapshots are
    44	  generated with `task-board plan ... --save`.
    45	- Implementation requires explicit user approval of the saved plan. The current
    46	  planning effort does not authorize implementation.

